# §0. Headline

**The leading cubic model is exactly scale-invariant. The entire r-ladder in GP-RSP-016 §6 was, mathematically, one computation repeated six times — and therefore the crossover at small r cannot be physics.**

Under the substitution \((x,y)=(rX,rY)\), \(Q=qr\), the cubic phase portrait is r-free. Every trajectory-determined classifier — adjacency, escape, the stable-root screen, the type indicator — is a function of \((q,a,w,z)\) alone. Consequently, in GP's exact experimental design, the true complements obey **exact power laws with analytic corrections**:

\[
\text{unweighted}(r)=C_1\,r\,(1+O(r)),\qquad
\text{weighted}(r)=C_3\,r^3\,(1+O(r)).
\]

No knee, no crossover, no slope drift beyond the \((1+O(r))\) factor is possible in exact arithmetic. The observed break between \(r=0.025\) and \(r=0.0125\) is a measurement artifact with a **7.5σ internal signature** (§3), and GP-PRE-015's R5-INCONCLUSIVE can be upgraded: the cubic-model question is now settled analytically, and the compute should move to the full-field comparison (GP-RSP-016 §9), which my theorem does not touch.

This also collapses the decisive computation: one r-free ensemble plus one-dimensional reweighting reproduces every rung with shared variance and zero stiffness (§4).

