# §1. Theorem and proof

**Theorem (cubic scale-invariance).** Let

\[
P_r(x,y)=b+\frac{x^3}3-\frac{r^2x}4-\frac{r^3}{12}
+\frac a2\Bigl(x^2-\frac{r^2}4\Bigr)y+\frac Q2y^2+\frac w2xy^2+\frac z6y^3
\]

be GP-RSP-016 §4's model. Under \(x=rX\), \(y=rY\), \(Q=qr\):

\[
P_r(rX,rY)=b+r^3\,\tilde P(X,Y;a,q,w,z),
\]
\[
\tilde P=\frac{X^3}3-\frac X4-\frac1{12}
+\frac a2\Bigl(X^2-\frac14\Bigr)Y+\frac q2Y^2+\frac w2XY^2+\frac z6Y^3 .
\]

The ascent flow satisfies \(dX/d\tau=\tilde P_X\), \(dY/d\tau=\tilde P_Y\) with \(\tau=rt\) — a pure time reparametrization. Hence the phase portrait in \((X,Y)\), and every classifier defined on it, depends only on \((q,a,w,z)\).

**Proof.** Term-by-term: \(x^3/3-r^2x/4-r^3/12=r^3(X^3/3-X/4-1/12)\); \((a/2)(x^2-r^2/4)y=r^3(a/2)(X^2-\tfrac14)Y\); \((Q/2)y^2=(qr/2)r^2Y^2=r^3(q/2)Y^2\); \((w/2)xy^2=r^3(w/2)XY^2\); \((z/6)y^3=r^3(z/6)Y^3\). Pins verified: \(\tilde P(\mp\tfrac12,0)=0,\,-\tfrac16\) and \(\nabla\tilde P(\pm\tfrac12,0)=0\), matching \(f(M)=b\), \(f(S)=b-r^3/6\), \(\nabla f=0\). For the flow: \(\partial_xP_r=r^2\tilde P_X\) and \(dx/dt=r\,dX/dt\) give \(dX/dt=r\tilde P_X\); set \(\tau=rt\). \(\square\)

**Hessians.** \(D^2P_r=r\,\tilde D^2\tilde P\), so with

\[
\widetilde{\det}_M=-\Bigl(q-\frac w2\Bigr)-\frac{a^2}4,
\qquad
\widetilde{\det}_S=\Bigl(q+\frac w2\Bigr)-\frac{a^2}4,
\]

the Palm weight is \(W_{MS}=r^4\,\tilde w(q,a,w,z)\), \(\tilde w=|\widetilde{\det}_M\widetilde{\det}_S|\sim q^2\) as \(|q|\to\infty\). The type event \(\{H_M\prec0,\det H_S<0\}\) is likewise a function of \((q,a,w,z)\): as \(|q|\to\infty\) it reduces to \(q<0\), which recovers `01_CORE_PAIRING_THEOREM.md` §5's \(z_0=E[Q^2\mathbf 1_{Q<0}]\) exactly. Internal consistency check passed.

