# §2. Corollary — exact rung laws for GP's design

GP samples \((Q,a,w,z)\sim N((-b,0,0,0),\operatorname{diag}(2,2,2,6))\) **independently of r**. Write \(f_Q\) for the \(N(-b,2)\) density; \(f_Q(0)=e^{-b^2/4}/(2\sqrt\pi)=0.19680\) at \(b=6/5\). Let \(F(q,a,w,z)\) be the failure indicator. GP's data gives the failure set compact q-support: all failing weight at \(|q|\le4\).

Substituting \(Q=qr\) in the outer expectation (\(dQ=r\,dq\), and \(f_Q(qr)=f_Q(0)(1+O(r))\) on \(|q|\le4\)):

\[
P(\text{type}\wedge\text{fail})
=r\,f_Q(0)\!\int\!\bar F\,dq\,d\mu\;(1+O(r)),
\]
\[
E[W\,\mathbf 1_{\text{fail}}]
=r^5\,f_Q(0)\!\int\!\tilde w\,\bar F\,dq\,d\mu\;(1+O(r)),
\qquad
Z_r=r^2\bigl(z_0+O(r)\bigr),
\]

the last because \(\tilde w\sim q^2\) makes the substitution \(u=qr\) reproduce \(E[Q^2\cdot]\). Dividing:

\[
\boxed{\ \text{unweighted}(r)=C_1r(1+O(r)),\qquad \text{weighted}(r)=C_3r^3(1+O(r)).\ }
\]

Both constants are single integrals over one r-free ensemble. **There is no mechanism in this design for a slope change at small r.** GP's flat-region values estimate the constants: \(C_1\approx0.012\)–\(0.013\), \(C_3\approx5.5\)–\(6.2\times10^{-4}\). The four small-r rows should be discarded, not averaged in.

